==English==

[[File:Pick thickness.jpg|thumb|Measuring the '''thickness''' of a guitar [[pick]] with [[calipers]]. The measured thickness is 2.0 mm.]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|thiknesse|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|þicnes||thickness, viscosity, density, hardness; obscurity, cloud, darkness; thicket; depth, a thick body, anything thick or heavy|lang=ang}}, equivalent to {{suffix|thick|ness}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|es}}

# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The property of being [[thick]] (in dimension).
# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} A measure of how thick (in dimension) something is.
#: ''The '''thickness''' of the Earth's crust is varies from two to 70 kilometres.''
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} A layer.
#: ''We upholstered the seat with three '''thicknesses''' of cloth to make it more comfortable to sit on.''
# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The quality of being thick (in consistency).
#: ''Whip the cream until it reaches a good '''thickness'''.''
# {{context|uncountable|informal|lang=en}} The property of being thick (slow to understand).

